This product includes software developed by third parties. The components
listed below are either vendored into this repository or pulled in as ESP-IDF
managed components at build time.

================================================================================
1. CMSIS-DAP core  --  main/dap/  (DAP.c, DAP.h, DAP_vendor.c, SW_DP.c,
                                   JTAG_DP.c)
================================================================================
Origin : ARMmbed DAPLink (https://github.com/ARMmbed/DAPLink)
Port   : cherry-embedded/CherryDAP (https://github.com/cherry-embedded/CherryDAP)
License: Apache License 2.0

DAP.c, DAP.h, DAP_vendor.c and SW_DP.c are kept verbatim apart from the
PIN_DELAY_SLOW fix documented inline in DAP.h; DAP_config.h is NexLink's own
board definition.

JTAG_DP.c is taken from the same source (CMSIS-DAP Source, JTAG_DP.c V2.0.0,
1. December 2017) with one change: the four PIN_TCK_/PIN_TMS_ aliases it defines
upstream were moved into DAP_config.h, where ARM's reference configurations put
them.

main/swo_uart.c is NOT taken from DAPLink: ARM's SWO.c depends on a CMSIS
Driver_USART, which ESP-IDF does not provide. It reimplements the byte source on
the ESP-IDF UART driver while reproducing the CMSIS-DAP SWO command layer,
response encoding and error/status semantics of SWO.c V2.0.1 (29. March 2021).

================================================================================
2. CherryUSB  --  managed component (cherry-embedded/cherryusb 1.4.3)
================================================================================
Origin : https://github.com/cherry-embedded/CherryUSB
License: Apache License 2.0

Provides the USB device stack and the ESP32-S3 DWC2 controller driver behind
main/dap/dap_usb.c (WinUSB-facing CMSIS-DAP) and main/serial/usb_ttl.c
(CDC-ACM virtual COM). Pulled in via main/idf_component.yml, not vendored.

================================================================================
3. cJSON  --  managed component (espressif/cjson 1.7.15)
================================================================================
Origin : https://github.com/DaveGamble/cJSON
License: MIT

Used for JSON handling on the device side.

================================================================================
4. Upstream project
================================================================================
NexLink is a derivative work of ai-wireless-debugger:
    https://gitee.com/JasonYANG170/ai-wireless-debugger

The upstream project supplied the initial structure: WiFi manager, pin
configuration, the UART bridge, the SPI/I2C/PWM monitors, the HTTP status page,
the original LCD menu and the first MCP Server. NexLink retains that code under
the terms of the Apache License 2.0 together with this repository.
